[{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>A particle mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg is acted upon by a resultant force <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N has acceleration <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. In each case, find the unknown variable:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=0.8\\text{ kg}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=1.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=0.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=5\\text{ kg}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F=15\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=200\\text{ g}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=0.8\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F=0.8\\times1.6=1.28\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20=0.8m\\Rightarrow m=25\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15=5a\\Rightarrow a=3\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F=0.2\\times0.8=0.16\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q2","number":2,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> A particle of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg with forces acting on it as shown in the diagram below, is accelerating at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. In each case, state the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.67/questions/assets/diagrams/q2a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.67/questions/assets/diagrams/q2b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.67/questions/assets/diagrams/q2c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad Q-5\\times9.8=0\\Rightarrow Q=49\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad P-10=5\\times2\\Rightarrow P=20\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad Q-3\\times9.8=0\\Rightarrow Q=29.4\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad Q=29\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2SF -- AQA)</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"P-8=3\\times1.5\\Rightarrow P=12.5\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=6.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad Q-6.5\\times9.8=0\\Rightarrow Q=63.7\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q=64\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2SF -- AQA)</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad P-40=6.5\\times-3\\Rightarrow P=20.5\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q3","number":3,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=10\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> A particle of mass <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg with forces acting on it as shown in the diagram below, is accelerating at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. In each case, state the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.67/questions/assets/diagrams/q3a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.67/questions/assets/diagrams/q3b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.67/questions/assets/diagrams/q3c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad P-3\\times10=3\\times2\\Rightarrow P=36\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=40\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (1SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=7.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad P-7.5\\times10=7.5\\times1.5\\Rightarrow P=86.25\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=90\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (1SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=1.2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad P-1.2\\times10=1.2\\times-0.8\\Rightarrow P=11.04\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (1SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>A particle of mass 2 kg is attached to the end of a light, vertical string. The particle is accelerating vertically at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. In each case find the tension in the string when:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=3\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> upwards.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=1.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> downwards.</p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=-2.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> upwards.</p></li><li><p>moving with constant velocity.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad T-2\\times10=2\\times3\\Rightarrow T=26\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=30\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (1SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad T-2\\times10=2\\times-1.5\\Rightarrow T=17\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (1SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad T-2\\times10=2\\times-2.5\\Rightarrow T=15\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (1SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad T-2\\times10=2\\times0\\Rightarrow T=20\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>A particle of mass 0.5 kg is attached to the end of a light, vertical string. The particle is decelerating upwards at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.2\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the tension in the string.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad T-0.5\\times10=0.5\\times-0.2\\Rightarrow T=4.9\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (1SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q6","number":6,"question":"<p><strong>The following questions use <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g=9.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></strong> A block of mass 8 kg is moving in a straight line with constant acceleration <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.1\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The force driving it forward is 12 N. Find the total resistance acting against the motion of the block.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad12-R=8\\times0.1\\Rightarrow R=11.2\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>A box is being pushed on a horizontal surface such that it is moving with constant velocity. The pushing force is 100 N. Find the total resistive force.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad100-R=m\\times0\\Rightarrow R=100\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>A box is being pushed on a horizontal smooth surface by a 24 N force so that it is accelerating at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the weight of the box.</p></li><li><p>State a modelling assumption used in your calculation.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad24=m\\times1.5\\Rightarrow m=16\\text{ kg}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad16\\times9.8-w=0\\Rightarrow w=156.8\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w=160\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The box is a particle OR the box is rigid OR the force pushing the box is parallel to the floor</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>A lorry of mass 3 tonnes is driving along a straight road. The lorry is experiencing resistance forces of 900 N. The engine is driving forward with a force of 2100 N. Find the acceleration of the lorry.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad2100-900=3000a\\Rightarrow a=0.4\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>A pebble of mass 50 g is falling to solid ground through a still body of water. The pebble is experiencing a downwards acceleration of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the total resistive forces acting on the pebble.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\downarrow):\\quad0.05\\times9.8-F=0.05\\times2.5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Total resistive force is 0.365 N</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F=0.37\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N (2SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>A car of mass 2000 kg reduces its speed from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"18\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to rest in 5 seconds, along a straight flat road.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the breaking force required to achieve this.</p></li><li><p>State the modelling assumption you have made in calculating the breaking force.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"0=18+5a\\Rightarrow a=-3.6\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad F=2000\\times-3.6\\Rightarrow F=-7200\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>That is a breaking force of 7200 N</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>There are no other external forces acting on the car. The car is modelled as a particle. The acceleration is uniform.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>A vehicle of mass 900 kg reduces its speed from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to rest in 6 seconds, along a straight flat road. It experiences a resistive force of 450 N during this time. Find the breaking force of the vehicle.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"0=20+6a\\Rightarrow a=-\\frac{10}{3}\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad F-450=900\\times-\\frac{10}{3}\\Rightarrow F=-2550\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>That is a breaking force of 2550 N</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q13","number":13,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q13-Q18: Constant Acceleration formulae</strong> A stone of mass 400 g is dropped from a bridge and falls vertically. It hits the ground 1.5 seconds after being released. A constant resistance to motion of the stone is given to be 2 N. Find the height from which the stone is dropped.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\downarrow):\\quad-2+0.4\\times9.8=0.4\\times a\\Rightarrow a=4.8\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"s=0+\\frac12\\times4.8\\times1.5^2=5.4\\text{ m}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>A body of weight 20 N is accelerating along rough horizontal ground, being pushed by a force of 7 N acting parallel to the ground. A constant resistance force of 5.5 N acts against the particle.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the mass of the particle.</p></li><li><p>Given the particle starts at rest, find its speed after 10 seconds.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"20=9.8m\\Rightarrow m=\\frac{100}{49}=2.04\\text{ kg (3 SF)}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m=2.0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> kg (2SF -- AQA)</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad7-5.5=\\frac{100}{49}\\times a\\Rightarrow a=0.735\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"v=0+0.735\\times10=7.35\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=7.4\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2SF -- AQA)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>A block of mass 3 kg starts at rest and is accelerating across a smooth horizontal ground by a force of 1.5 N acting parallel to the ground. Find how far it has travelled in the first 4 seconds of motion.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad1.5=3\\times a\\Rightarrow a=0.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"s=0+\\frac12\\times0.5\\times4^2=4\\text{ metres}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>A car of mass 1650 kg is driving with constant speed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when it begins accelerating. After 30 m it reaches a speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"18\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the resultant force acting on the car during the period of acceleration.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"18^2=10^2+2\\times a\\times30\\Rightarrow a=\\frac{56}{15}=3.73\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad F=1650\\times\\frac{56}{15}\\Rightarrow F=6160\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>A car of mass 2000 kg is driving at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"47\\text{ km h}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when the driver notices an accident ahead. When the car is 20 metres away from the accident, the driver applies the brakes creating a total resistance force of 10 000 N. Determine whether the car stops before the accident.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad-10000=2000\\times a\\Rightarrow a=-5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"u=47\\text{ km h}^{-1}\\Rightarrow\\frac{235}{18}\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"0=\\left(\\frac{235}{18}\\right)^2+2\\times-5\\times s\\Rightarrow s=17.0\\text{ m}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So the car stops in time.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.67-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>A van of mass 2250 kg drives a distance of 40 metres along a straight road, accelerating uniformly from rest to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the acceleration of the van.</p></li><li><p>the magnitude of the force exerted by the engine, stating any modelling assumptions you have made in this calculation.</p></li><li><p>the magnitude of the normal reaction between the van and the road.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"25^2=0^2+2a\\times40\\Rightarrow a=7.8125\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\rightarrow):\\quad F=2250\\times7.8125\\Rightarrow F=17\\,578.125\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F=17\\,600\" data-display=\"false\"></span> N</p>","<p>This calculates the total force in the direction of motion so the assumption is that there is no resistance to motion such as friction from the road and air resistance. The van is also modelled as particle and is assumed to be rigid.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{R}(\\uparrow):\\quad R-2250\\times9.8=0\\Rightarrow R=22050\\text{ N}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R=22000\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (2SF -- AQA)</p>"]}]